# Paths excluded from the Cloudflare static-asset upload (gitignore syntax,
# relative to the asset directory = repo root). Everything NOT listed here is
# published, so new generated artifacts are served by default.
#
# Served on purpose: index.html, 404.html, llms.txt, llms-full.txt, robots.txt,
# sitemap.xml, openapi.yaml, health.json, api/, l/, listings/, assets/.
#
# EVERY ENTRY HERE IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and new ones must be too.
# These are gitignore patterns: unanchored, they match at every depth, not just
# the repo root. The bare `mcp` line below once excluded `api/mcp/` as well as
# the top-level `mcp/` it was written for, so the whole MCP catalog 404'd in
# production while CI stayed green — the build was right, the upload was short.
# `node_modules` is the one deliberate exception: it should vanish at any depth.
/.git
/.github
/.gitignore
/.nojekyll
/.assetsignore
node_modules
/scripts
/templates
/worker
/docs
/mcp
/clients
# The Clustly listing: the text of a service sold on someone else's marketplace,
# plus the pricing reasoning behind it (what the comparable listings charge, and
# why this one opens below them). Entered into their console by hand — nothing
# here is served, and the commercial reasoning is not for publication.
/clustly
/wrangler.toml
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/site.config.json
# Registry metadata and the stdio server's build spec — read by Glama off the
# GitHub repo, never served by the site.
/glama.json
/Dockerfile
/README.md
/TODO.md
/NEXT.md
/DEPLOY.md
/ARCHITECTURE.md
/result.md
/health-report.md
/payments.json
# `wrangler dev` writes local state here, including the contents of the local
# KV namespace. The asset directory is the repo root, so without this line a
# deploy from a machine that has ever run `wrangler dev` publishes it.
/.wrangler

